    <chapter>
      <heading>TTIOTransportPacket functions</heading>
      <p></p>
      <function type="uint32_t" name="TTIOTransportCRC32C">
        <arg type="const uint8_t*">data</arg>
        <arg type="NSUInteger">length</arg>
        <desc>
          CRC-32C (Castagnoli, reflected). Used when
          TTIOTransportPacketFlagHasChecksum
          is set on a packet header. Matches google-crc32c and
          java.util.zip.CRC32C output. @param
          <var>data</var> Pointer to the bytes to hash. @param
          <var>length</var> Number of bytes available at
          ``data``. @return The 32-bit CRC-32C value as a
          little-endian integer.
        </desc>
      </function>
      <function type="BOOL" name="TTIOTransportIsKnownPacketType">
        <arg type="uint8_t">typeByte</arg>
        <desc>
          Returns ``YES`` iff ``typeByte`` names a defined
          ``TTIOTransportPacketType``.
          Used by the reader's forward-compat skip-unknown path
          (transport-spec §6) — decoded headers whose
          ``packetTypeByte`` fails this check are
          length-prefix skipped rather than rejected.
          Cross-language parity: Java
          ``PacketType.fromWireOrNull``,
          Python ``is_known_packet_type``. @param
          <var>typeByte</var> Wire byte read out of the header's
          packet-type field. @return ``YES`` when the byte
          names a known type; ``NO`` otherwise.
        </desc>
      </function>
